# Build context for docker/runner-cuda-sm90.Dockerfile.
#
# A deny-list, unlike the allow-list the test-time-bench template uses. That
# template's images are named by a hash of an enumerated file set, so it has to
# know exactly which paths are inputs. This build compiles a Cargo workspace with
# `cargo install --path bin/pie`, whose input is the whole tree; an allow-list
# would have to restate the workspace and would silently break on any new crate.
#
# Excluded here is only what must not reach a build: local build output, secrets,
# and directories large enough to slow the context upload for no benefit.

.git
.gitignore

# Rust and CMake output, at the root and in any nested crate.
target
**/target

# Node output under website/ and the SDK tooling.
**/node_modules

# Local logs and scratch.
logs
**/*.log

# Never ship credentials into a build context.
**/*.env
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*

# The ignore files themselves are not build inputs.
**/*.dockerignore

# Neither is the build tooling. pie is compiled from the Cargo workspace, and the
# Dockerfile is read by the client through -f rather than out of the context, so
# excluding these changes nothing about what gets built. Leaving them in couples
# the recipe to the cache key of `COPY . .`, which means editing a comment in this
# Dockerfile recompiles the CUDA driver from scratch — 31 minutes for no reason.
#
# docker/runpod-sshd-entrypoint.sh deliberately stays: the runtime stage COPYs it.
docker/*.Dockerfile
scripts/build-runner-image.sh
